Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:01:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 54/62] hjviewer: ui: dialogs-account: dialog contents, the
 login, the account and update screens

The dialogs' contents follow the look of the home screens (common/hjv_style.dart); the
wrapper itself (CustomAlertDialog, msgbox, dialogButton) is in common.dart and stays as it is.

- dialog.dart: a field's label sits above it (hjvFieldLabel, used by DialogTextField and the
  dialogs' own fields), its icon quiet until the field has the focus, the password's eye
  grey; a title with an icon is left-aligned, the icon in the accent or, for a destructive
  action, the danger colour (HjvDialogTitle); an explanation below a title is 14 px in the
  secondary text colour (hjvDialogTextStyle); the 2FA code on a white tile with the cards'
  border; the elevation note, the ID rules and the shared password's warning from the
  palette; [Close]/[Cancel] first in the trusted devices and end-of-connection dialogs,
  [Delete] in the danger colour.
- login.dart: the login dialog at a fixed width, its title and a quiet close button on one
  line, the login button across it, and the failed login options as a quiet block with
  [Retry].
- hjviewer_account.dart: the pilot notice, this PC's lines, the PC password hint and the wake
  hints as quiet blocks; the logged-in devices as list cards under a section label; the
  device list banners as rounded callouts; removing and logging out in the danger colour.
- hjv_update.dart: the update screen as a centred card like the connect box, its buttons
  across it; the banner as a rounded callout; About's update lines as a block; the notice
  over a session as a floating card.

No behaviour, texts, translate() keys or widget keys change; the widget tests of these
screens pass unchanged.

After an independent review (screens in light and dark, the diff, the code rules):

- Phone dialogs of the account and update screens: _button draws the quiet button in the
  secondary colour and the action in bold, as dialogButton() does since the shared commit.
- One quiet note block (hjvNoteBlock, dialog.dart) for the pilot notice, the failed login
  options, the PC password hint, the wake hints and the elevation note; the raw login error
  at 12 px in the secondary colour. The login dialog is 440 px wide so that it still fits an
  800x600 window with both notes, and its close button is a 44 px target on phones.
- Filled destructive buttons in dangerFill (OK of the delete confirmation, Remove, Delete);
  on a phone the delete OK and Remove in the danger colour.
- Desktop Settings > Account: the panel sits at the content margin, takes no room when it is
  empty, and its buttons are 36 px like the settings' own; the wake checkbox lines up with
  the other checkboxes. About: the update buttons are 36 px.
- The phone settings tiles of these files use Pretendard; the wake row toggles from anywhere
  on it off an iPhone and has the rounded icon.
- Logged-in devices on a phone: the log-out button sits below the device's line.
- The device list's banners match buildErrorBanner; the update strip takes the fields'
  radius; a dialog whose only text is its question shows it in the text colour.

No behaviour, texts, translate() keys or widget keys change; the widget tests pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
